  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Kishan Singh vs Venkatesh And Another on 5 June, 2025 Kabc0C0086032021 Presented on : 03-06-2021 Registered on : 03-06-2021 Decided on : 05-06-2025 Duration : 4 years, 0 month, 2 days In The Court Of The Xxix Addl.C.M.M Mayohall Unit, Bengaluru -: Present :- Sri. Girish Chatni, B.A., LL.B(Spl) Xxix Addl. Chief Metropolitan Magistrate, Bengaluru. Dated: This the 05th Day of June, 2025 Criminal Case No.52558/2021 The State by H.A.L., Police Station. ... Complainant. (By Learned Assistant Public Prosecutor) // Versus // 1. Venkatesh S/o Late.Ananthappa, Aged about 38 years, R/at: No.1, Golden Enclave Main Road, Banjara Layout, Horamavu, Bengaluru. 2 C.C.No.52558/2021 2. Raju S/o Chikkona, Aged about 30 years, R/at: Malala Pattana Village, Koodluru Post, Channapattana Taluk, Ramanagara District. ... Accused (By Sri.P.M, Advocate) Kishan Singh vs Venkatesh And Another on 5 June, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/63960965/ 1 Date of commission of offence : 15.03.2020 Date of report of offence : 16.03.2020 Name of the complainant : Kishan Singh Date of recording evidence : 15.05.2025 Date of closing evidence : 15.05.2025 Sec.304A of Ipc. Offences complained of : Opinion of the Judge : Accused No.1 & 2 found not guilty. (Girish Chatni) Xxix Acjm, Bengaluru 3 C.C.No.52558/2021 Judgment",
    "facts": "The P.S.I., of H.A.L., Police Station, Bengaluru, has filed the present charge sheet against the accused No.1 and 2 for the offence punishable under section 304A of Indian Penal Code. 2. BRIEF FACTS OF THE PROSECUTION CASE ARE AS UNDER : It is the case of the complainant that, accused No.1 is running a Udupi Vaibhava Hotel, near Marathahalli Bridge, HAL and accused No.2 is working as a Manager in the said Hotel. It is further alleged that, on 06.03.2020 accused persons appointed the deceased Ganesh as server and on 15.03.2020 at about 8.45 PM, the said deceased Ganesh went in a temporary lift from ground floor to first floor in the said hotel to serve the food , by that time, he was struck in the said temporary lift and succumbed to death due to the negligent act of accused No.1 and 2 in not making proper and safety requirements towards the said lift. Based on the written complaint lodged by C.W.1, C.W.17 has registered the case against accused No.1 and 2 in P.S. Crime No.101/2020 for the offence punishable under section 304A of IPC. Investigating Officer/CW.17 investigated C.C.No.52558/2021 the matter and after completion of the investigation has submitted final report against the accused for the offence punishable under section 304A of IPC. 3. Upon receipt of charge sheet, cognizance was taken for the above said offence alleged against the accused No.1 and 2 and registered the criminal case against them. 4. After registering the case, the accused No.1 and 2 have appeared before the court and were released on bail. Copies of the final report and its' enclosures were furnished to them in compliance Kishan Singh vs Venkatesh And Another on 5 June, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/63960965/ 2 of section 207 of Cr.P.C. Substance of accusation read over to the accused No.1 and 2. They pleaded not guilty and claimed to be tried. 5. In order to prove the guilt of the accused persons, the prosecution has examined one witness out of 17 witnesses cited in the charge sheet as P.W.1 and relied upon documents as per Ex.P.1 to Ex.P.5 and closed its side. In lieu of absence of incriminating circumstances appearing against accused persons, recording of their statement under section 313 of Cr.P.C. was dispensed with.",
